        "title": "Graphic Design - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "This volume collects four fields that appear unrelated until you see the shared\noperation: reduction. A graphic designer eliminates visual noise until hierarchy\nemerges. A comics artist eliminates drawn moments until the reader's imagination\nfills the gap. A fashion editor eliminates garments from a collection until a\nsilhouette thesis crystallizes. A sports scientist eliminates wasted motion until\nperformance converges on signal."
    },
